  "analysis": {
    "summary": "A three-note motif is stated over {{chord 1}} and then restated on every chord, keeping its rhythm and its falling shape. Only the notes that no longer fit move, each by a step to the nearest note of the new chord, and those moves are the guide tones: the b7 of {{chord 1}} falls to the 3rd of {{chord 2}}, and the b7 of {{chord 2}} falls to the 3rd of {{chord 3}}. The last statement comes in early, so it lands on the downbeat of {{chord 4}}.",
