        "text": "The first three statements start on the 'and' of one and hold their last note over beat three, with a rest after each one. The fourth statement starts on beat four instead, so its last note lands squarely on the downbeat of {{chord 4}}. Moving a motif to a new place in the bar like this is called rhythmic displacement."
      },
      {
